{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaConnect Router now supports high bitrate mode - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaConnect Router has recently added support for high bitrate modes with two new tiers: 250 Mbps and 500 Mbps. This update caters to professional broadcasters requiring higher bitrates for transporting high-value content without sacrificing quality or reliability. The new feature enables industry-standard workflows such as VSF TR-07 compliant transport stream distribution for broadcast contribution, content distribution, and remote production. High bitrate mode offers redundancy with up to two sources for enhanced reliability and includes data plane optimizations to minimize jitter for improved performance. For more information, visit the AWS Elemental MediaConnect product page and pricing page","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/10/mediaconnect-router-high-bitrate/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"aws-media-services","skill_description":"Designs, deploys, reviews, evaluates, audits, and troubleshoots video streaming workflows across AWS media services (MediaConnect, MediaLive, MediaConvert, MediaPackage v2, MediaTailor, CloudFront). Includes per-service validation rules, cross-service workflow patterns for live streaming, linear channels, VOD pipelines, and live-to-VOD, service-specific troubleshooting, best practices assessment, cost optimization, encoder settings, DRM, SCTE-35 ad insertion, epoch locking, and CDN cache configuration.\n\nServices: mediaconnect, medialive, mediaconvert, mediapackage, mediatailor, cloudfront\nTasks: review, deploy, troubleshoot, audit, optimize\nPersona: video-engineer, solutions-architect\nWorkload: live-streaming, vod, linear-channel","skill_name":"aws-media-services"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"aws-marketplace-metering","skill_description":"Deploys, queries, and debugs AWS Marketplace usage-based (PAYG) metering — the pipeline (ResolveCustomer, BatchMeterUsage, EventBridge via SAM) and querying/debugging metering records, statuses, failures, discrepancies. Covers Concurrent Agreements (CustomerAWSAccountId + LicenseArn), multi-product, CloudTrail Event History (90 days; never CloudTrail Lake), Seller Reports (Billed Revenue/Usage columns + CSV/SDDS parsing), existing-stack detection, metering region for BatchMeterUsage/MeterUsage (DisabledApiException), metered AMI/Container + IAM roles, where registration data lives (customer-profile table), legacy ProductCode + CustomerIdentifier, DuplicateRecord/CustomerNotSubscribed, bad LicenseArn. Also SCOPES adjacent asks — flat-rate/SaaS-Subscription \"do I still meter\", CCP included-units + overage, contract term/annual renewal, forecasting future bills/usage — with the right answer or a one-line redirect. Use for any BatchMeterUsage/ResolveCustomer or SaaS usage-billing question.\n\nServices: aws-marketplace, marketplace-metering\nTasks: deploy, integrate, query, debug, troubleshoot, analyze\nPersona: developer\nWorkload: saas\n*","skill_name":"aws-marketplace-metering"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"testing-mwaa-workflow","skill_description":"Tests Amazon MWAA workflow execution end-to-end: trigger a run and monitor it to completion for Provisioned (Python DAG, via Airflow REST API) and Serverless (YAML workflow, via StartWorkflowRun). Verifies the artifact is deployed and parse-ready, triggers with confirmation, polls to terminal state, and on failure delegates diagnosis to debugging-mwaa-workflow and artifact/redeploy fixes to authoring-mwaa-workflow, then retests up to a capped number of attempts. Triggers on: test my DAG, test my workflow, run my DAG, trigger a test run, does my DAG work, smoke-test the pipeline, verify my workflow runs, execute my DAG to check it. Not applicable to writing or deploying a new workflow (handled by authoring-mwaa-workflow), or for diagnosing why a run failed or root-causing an error (handled by debugging-mwaa-workflow).\n\n\nServices: mwaa\nTasks: test\nPersona: data-engineer\nWorkload: analytics, orchestration\n*","skill_name":"testing-mwaa-workflow"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search AWS docs for MediaConnect SourceBitRate metric and color bars test content", "parent_id": "439dbb67-ff0b-4fa6-8b4e-24c4c92295e3"}
